another  reality of the  covet 19 pandemic is how it's going to  affect the draft the draft is going  forward it doesn't matter what we or  anyone else say the draft is happening  for a variety of reasons now the  challenge is how do you make the  selection process mesh with the  requirements  that are in place for  39 states and rising to stay at home  shelter in place only leave your home  for essential purposes and chris one  thing that  i recognized last night with a nudge  from somebody who was paying closer  attention to it than i was  when the nfl says we're going to allow  small gatherings of up to 10  for these mini war rooms for the draft  that's not going to fly in some of these  states if not all of these states where  the order is stay at home except for  essential purposes and those states  would very likely say it's not essential  for you to go get together in a group of  ten you can do it from home you don't  need to leave the house to go to some  location to have your draft war room and  i don't know the nfl is paying attention  to that issue and it may be that at the  end of the day the nfl has to backtrack  on it and say we can't do this because  if we can't if we can't do it in every  state that has a stay-at-home order then  it creates an unfair advantage for the  teams that can do it and i think  ultimately there's a chance they're just  going to pull the plug and say sorry you  can't you can't gather anywhere you're  going to have to do the draft entirely  from home everybody's going to have to  be at home you cannot leave your house  to go somewhere to get together with  even a group of two or three people  well first off i mean the states that  don't have the stay at home order like i  want to just say what what you are going  to take 49 states for us to see this  issue and then the 50th states finally  to go you know we didn't do the  stay-at-home order and everything  exploded like come on america what are  we doing like i just i don't understand  it you know all those spring breakers  that were down in florida they have  traveled back to their homes all over  the country so we got to worry about  that too but i'm with you and then this  is again an example mike of where the  nfl needs to be careful and they need to  show leadership to society in these type  of moments and if we're still here at  draft time and we're still in the kind  of the current state we are right now  where we're social distancing and not  that many people are allowed to gather  in one place then they need to  set the right example and not do that  added to the fact mike as you know and  you just said it you know you don't need  10 people in the war room for the draft  i mean at the end of the day you need  the owner the gm the head coach  the director of pro personnel and maybe  your head college scout everybody else  okay can call in or video conference and  i'm not even sure you need all five of  those guys you could probably just get  away with the owner the head coach and  the gm and have the other guys call in  too so that to me if that's where we're  at at that point you know the nfl needs  to be careful and make sure they do the  right thing and how it looks on the  optics and set a good example  how it looks is the key chris you said  the key words how it looks because it's  not going to look as good if everyone is  at home and it's all on zoom or face  time and they're connecting that way and  that's what gets shown on tv they still  want to be able to show  gatherings of jerry jones and stephen  jones and mike mccarthy  you know passing a phone around to the  to the as they're talking to the guy  that they make their first round pick  they want it to look normal in that way  it's not going to look normal in that  way not if the nfl properly complies  with the requirements of the states  where the stay-at-home order is in place  and and it sends a bad message to the  rest of us if the nfl is going to try to  try to twist and warp the rules to  justify having these war rooms in the  states with stay-at-home orders you know  we all should be complying to these  rules to the letter we shouldn't be  leaving the home for any reason that  truly isn't essential and uh i'm just  i have a feeling this one isn't over and  it's got three weeks to play out i think  by the time it's all said and done  everybody's going to be required to be  at home for the draft the coaches at  home the gm's at home everyone at home  okay well what if what if they found  some way to you know test everybody you  know two days before the draft and they  kind of kept them quarantined in the  facility if it was four or five people  and just say hey you know we've tested  you you're here now you gotta stay here  we're not letting you involved with  society and we'll see where it goes i  mean could they pull something like that  off  you're gonna have to take it up with 39  different uh states or at least the 22  states where the nfl does business and  make sure that it doesn't violate the  stay-at-home order to put those people  in the same place so there's there's a  lot of elbow grease they're gonna have  to put in to make this work and make it  mesh and i don't know that that issue's  on their radar screen well if it wasn't  it is now  hi i'm mike tarico and thanks for  watching make sure to hit subscribe for  the latest news and highlights from nbc  sports

